{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>In the pillar of cloud, to them</b> — It reverts to Moses and Aaron, and Samuel is not with them, like וישם דמי מלחמה בשלום (2 Samuel 20:12), where it reverts to Joab alone and not Amasa, and many like it. And the meaning of 'concerning Moses and Aaron' — that they are keepers of His testimonies, is because they are intermediaries between HaShem and Israel, and the testimonies and statutes that HaShem gave them they kept to say them thus to Israel and not add and not subtract, and this is their praise, for there is no need to mention of them that they kept the Torah." "<b>Exalt</b> — when you come to the Temple." "<b>And bow down to His footstool</b> — opposite the place of the Ark, for the place of His footstool is holy. Or it reverts to HaShem who is honored, as written at the end of the psalm." "<b>Moses in the pillar</b> — I have explained it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 99, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:37.886092507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}